"GhostTuning.hud_relocated_message_duration": "How long the HUD's \"relocated into your territory\" auto-drop message stays fully visible before it starts fading.",
"GhostTuning.hud_relocated_fade_duration": "How long the HUD's relocated message takes to fade out.",
"GhostTuning.spawn_clearance": "Small extra gap added on top of the minimal raise that lifts a new block clear of a placed block it would spawn inside.",
"GhostTuning.spawn_clearance_step": "Search step (metres) when finding how far to raise a block that spawns inside another.",
"GhostTuning.spawn_clearance_max_raise": "Largest spawn-clearance raise (metres) applied to one new block.",
"GhostTuning.spawn_clearance_bisect_steps": "Refinement passes that trim the spawn-clearance raise down to the minimum.",
"GhostTuning.spawn_clearance_decay_speed": "Metres per second a spawn-clearance raise settles back to your own hover once it is no longer needed.",
"GhostTuning.spawn_clearance_settle_timeout_s": "Longest wait (seconds) for a just-dropped block under the new held block to come to rest before deciding whether the new block needs raising.",
"GhostTuning.spawn_clearance_enabled": "Raise the next held block just enough to clear a block it would spawn inside (off: it spawns at normal hover height).",
"GhostTuning.throw_aim_tint_color": "Ghost tint shown while aiming a throw (holding throw_aim on a held special).",
"GhostTuning.throw_arc_sample_count": "Number of straight segments the throw-aim arc preview is divided into before its own landing cutoff can stop it early.",
"GhostTuning.throw_arc_max_time_s": "Safety-cap seconds of flight the throw-aim arc preview samples out to if it never reaches a landing height at all.",
"GhostTuning.throw_arc_color": "Colour of the throw-aim arc preview line and its landing-point marker.",
"GhostTuning.throw_arc_width": "World-space width, in meters, of the throw-aim arc preview's ribbon.",
"GhostTuning.throw_arc_floor_below_disc_m": "How far below the disc's surface the throw-aim arc preview lands once its XZ has flown past the disc's rim.",
"GhostTuning.throw_arc_floor_enabled": "Whether an off-disc throw-aim arc preview lands on throw_arc_floor_below_disc_m at all, instead of falling until the safety cap.",
"GhostTuning.throw_arc_end_marker_enabled": "Whether the throw-aim arc preview drops a small marker disc at its own landing point.",
"GhostTuning.throw_arc_end_marker_radius": "World-space radius, in meters, of the throw-aim arc preview's landing-point marker disc.",
"PhysicsTuning.cube_size": "Edge length of one physics cube, in meters.",
"PhysicsTuning.cube_margin": "How much each cube's collision box shrinks so neighboring blocks don't jam together.",
"PhysicsTuning.cube_mass": "Mass of one physics cube; a shape's total mass is its cube count times this.",
"PhysicsTuning.block_friction": "Friction of a block's physics material.",
"PhysicsTuning.block_bounce": "Bounciness (restitution) of a block's physics material.",
"PhysicsTuning.block_linear_damp": "Linear damping applied to every block's rigid body; higher values slow falling blocks faster.",
"PhysicsTuning.block_angular_damp": "Angular damping applied to every block's rigid body; higher values slow tumbling blocks faster.",
"PhysicsTuning.disk_friction": "Friction of the playing field's disk surface.",
"PhysicsTuning.kill_plane_y": "World Y height below which any physics body is freed.",
"PhysicsTuning.hover_height": "Height above the surface the ghost preview hovers while aiming a placement.",
"PhysicsTuning.sleep_linear_threshold": "Linear speed below which a block counts as settled for territory rules.",
"PhysicsTuning.sleep_angular_threshold": "Angular speed below which a block counts as settled for territory rules.",
"PhysicsTuning.sleep_settle_time": "How long a block must stay below both settle thresholds before it counts as settled.",
"PhysicsTuning.gravity_multiplier": "Multiplier on world gravity applied to blocks.",
"PhysicsTuning.lobby_gravity_baseline": "Factor multiplied by the lobby gravity setting at match start to give the effective gravity_multiplier (lobby 1.0 = this).",
"PhysicsTuning.rebound_damping": "Multiplies a block's upward velocity only on the one physics step a fall turns into a bounce, so it doesn't fly straight back up; 1 leaves every bounce untouched, lower values damp the straight-up rebound while leaving sideways/tumbling motion from block_bounce alone.",
"PhysicsTuning.stable_freeze_delay_s": "How long (seconds) a block must be asleep without moving before the host freezes it to a static body; a wake that moves it restarts the count.",
"PhysicsTuning.stable_freeze_rest_epsilon_m": "How far (meters) a woken block may shift from the pose it fell asleep in and still keep its stable-freeze timer; 0 restarts the timer on every wake.",
"PhysicsTuning.stable_freeze_scan_interval_s": "How often (seconds) the host scans for asleep blocks to freeze static; lower values notice sleep/wake sooner at a small extra scan cost.",
"TerritoryTuning.influence_base": "Base radius of a block's territory influence circle before height scaling.",
"TerritoryTuning.influence_k": "How much a block's height above the disk adds to its territory influence radius.",
"TerritoryTuning.influence_max_fraction": "Maximum influence-circle radius, as a fraction of the field radius.",
"TerritoryTuning.home_radius": "Radius of a home flag's own permanent influence circle.",
"TerritoryTuning.max_circles": "Maximum influence circles kept live at once; extra small circles are dropped in favor of the largest per team.",
"TerritoryTuning.solve_hz": "How many times per second territory ownership is recomputed.",
"TerritoryTuning.raster_upload_hz": "How many times per second the territory raster/circle list is uploaded for rendering and networking.",
"TerritoryTuning.solve_defer_max_s": "While any block is still moving, territory solves wait until everything settles, but never longer than this many seconds; 0 solves on every tick regardless.",
"TerritoryTuning.async_solve_min_circles": "Boards with at least this many territory circles are solved on a background thread and applied one frame later; 0 always solves on the main thread.",
"TerritoryTuning.dirty_move_epsilon": "How far (metres) a settled block must move before territory is recomputed; an unchanged board skips the solve entirely.",
"TerritoryTuning.hash_cell_size": "Size of the spatial-hash cells used to speed up territory circle overlap checks.",
"TerritoryTuning.hole_delay": "How long a cell must stay contested before it becomes a hole.",
"TerritoryTuning.hole_close_delay": "How long a temporary hole stays open after the contest that created it ends.",
"TerritoryTuning.max_cell_toggles_per_frame": "Maximum territory cells allowed to change ownership in a single frame.",
"TerritoryTuning.goal_zone_radius": "Radius of the no-build zone around every goal flag.",
"TerritoryTuning.capture_hold": "How long one connected territory must contain every goal flag to win.",
"TerritoryTuning.ctf_score_per_beacon_second": "Capture the Flag: points a team earns per second for each beacon it holds.",
"TerritoryTuning.ctf_replicate_interval_s": "Capture the Flag: seconds between score replications to clients; a held-beacon change replicates immediately.",
"TerritoryTuning.sky_replicate_interval_s": "Reach the Sky: minimum seconds between height-record replications to clients; the first change after a quiet spell replicates at once.",
"TerritoryTuning.domination_replicate_interval_s": "Domination: minimum seconds between territory-share replications to clients; the final shares always go out at the round end.",
"TerritoryTuning.auto_drop_search_step": "Distance between each ring of the spiral search used to auto-drop a block to the nearest valid spot.",
"TerritoryTuning.auto_drop_search_max_radius": "Maximum distance the auto-drop spiral search looks before falling back to a full scan of the player's own territory; only an empty territory still throws the block off the map.",
"TerritoryTuning.reject_impulse": "Strength of the impulse applied to a block that's thrown off the map for an invalid placement.",
"TerritoryTuning.reject_upward_fraction": "Fraction of the reject impulse aimed straight up; the rest points radially outward from the disk center.",
"TerritoryTuning.sudden_death_ramp_s": "Seconds after sudden death starts for the special-gift chance to climb from the match setting to the maximum of the spawn model, then hold there.",
"TerritoryTuning.sudden_death_shrink_interval_s": "Seconds between each sudden-death crumble of the disk edge (spec: 1 m every 10 s).",
"TerritoryTuning.sudden_death_shrink_step_m": "Metres the disk radius shrinks per sudden-death crumble; each ring becomes a permanent hole.",
"TerritoryTuning.sudden_death_tiebreak_radius_m": "Disk radius at which sudden death ends and the team with the most territory wins if nobody has won yet.",
"TerritoryTuning.turn_based_max_settle_s": "In turn-based mode, the longest a turn waits for every placed block to settle before handing play to the next player anyway.",
"TerritoryVisuals.disk_base_color": "Color of the disk surface where no team owns the ground.",
"TerritoryVisuals.disk_metallic": "Metallic value of the disk surface; higher darkens the lit territory tint and strengthens the sky/probe sheen (the planar mirror is mirror_strength).",
"TerritoryVisuals.disk_roughness": "Roughness of the disk's sky/probe/SSR sheen; lower makes that sheen sharper (the sun highlight is off on the disk).",
"TerritoryVisuals.disk_mesh_segments": "Radial segments in the disk mesh; higher makes the rim read as a circle rather than a polygon.",
"TerritoryVisuals.top_grain_strength": "Strength of the disc top's brushed/plank grain's NORMAL perturbation; nearly invisible in flat lighting, shows up as fine streaks in the sun sheen and reflections. 0 disables it.",
"TerritoryVisuals.top_grain_scale": "Spatial frequency (cycles per meter) of the disc top grain's coarse plank bands; higher reads as many narrow bands.",
"TerritoryVisuals.top_grain_fine_scale": "Multiplier on top_grain_scale for a finer brushed ripple layered inside each plank band.",
"TerritoryVisuals.top_grain_roughness_strength": "Strength of the disc top grain's small additive ROUGHNESS variation; 0 disables it.",
"TerritoryVisuals.disk_sky_sheen_color": "Color of the cool sky fresnel sheen on the disc top.",
"TerritoryVisuals.disk_sky_sheen_strength": "Strength of the cool sky fresnel sheen on the disc top (strongest at grazing angles).",
"TerritoryVisuals.disk_sky_sheen_power": "Fresnel exponent of the disc sky sheen; higher confines it to more grazing angles.",
"TerritoryVisuals.disk_fill_color": "Flat cool graphite fill of the disc top, independent of sky ambient light.",
"TerritoryVisuals.disk_ambient_scale": "Scale of the sky ambient light on the disc top (0 = none). Lower keeps the graphite from borrowing the sky colour.",
"TerritoryVisuals.disk_specular": "Dielectric reflectance of the disc top (0.5 = engine default). Lower makes the surface darker head-on while grazing angles still show the sky.",
"TerritoryVisuals.panel_size_m": "Edge length in meters of the disc top machined-panel tiles.",
"TerritoryVisuals.panel_seam_width_px": "Screen-space width in pixels of the seams between disc top panels.",
"TerritoryVisuals.panel_seam_strength": "How much the panel seams darken the disc top (0 = invisible).",
"TerritoryVisuals.panel_variation": "Per-panel brightness variation of the disc top (fraction of albedo).",
"TerritoryVisuals.panel_fade_px": "On-screen panel size in pixels below which the seams fade out to avoid moire.",
"TerritoryVisuals.tint_fill_emission": "Light-independent emissive fill of the territory tint, so it reads at the same strength in day and night themes.",
"TerritoryVisuals.disk_diffuse_response": "Overall energy of the disc top's direct-sunlight diffuse response; lower keeps the disc's own cool color from being overwhelmed by the sun's warm light.",
"TerritoryVisuals.disk_diffuse_desaturate": "How much the direct sunlight's own warm color is desaturated toward its luminance before lighting the disc top; 1.0 removes the hue entirely.",
"TerritoryVisuals.disk_sheen_color": "Color of the view-dependent sun sheen, brightest where the disc top mirrors the sun toward the camera.",
"TerritoryVisuals.disk_sheen_strength": "Peak strength of the sun sheen on the disc top; 0 disables it.",
"TerritoryVisuals.disk_sheen_exponent": "Shininess exponent shaping the sun sheen's falloff; lower is a broader, softer lobe, higher is a tighter highlight.",
"TerritoryVisuals.edge_softness": "How blurry the territory tint's edge is where ownership changes (raster fallback path only; see edge_softness_m for the ordinary analytic path).",
"TerritoryVisuals.edge_softness_m": "Half-width, in meters, of the ownership tint's own edge feather on the analytic (ordinary) rendering path; smaller is crisper. The rim glow's own softness is unaffected (see rim_soft_width/rim_width).",
"TerritoryVisuals.tint_alpha": "How strongly a team's color tints the disk at full territory coverage.",
"TerritoryVisuals.outline_width": "Width of the animated outline band drawn around a territory edge.",
"TerritoryVisuals.outline_speed": "Pulses per second of the territory outline's animation.",
"TerritoryVisuals.outline_strength": "Emission strength of the territory outline at the peak of its pulse.",
"TerritoryVisuals.outline_pulse_depth": "How much of the territory outline's brightness is animated versus a constant glow.",
"TerritoryVisuals.contested_color": "Color of the shimmer shown over contested cells.",
"TerritoryVisuals.contested_shimmer_rate": "Shimmer cycles per second over contested cells.",
"TerritoryVisuals.contested_shimmer_scale": "Spatial frequency of the contested-cell shimmer's traveling bands across the disk.",
"TerritoryVisuals.contested_shimmer_strength": "Intensity of the contested-cell shimmer effect.",
"TerritoryVisuals.hole_rim_color": "Color of the glowing rim drawn just outside a hole.",
"TerritoryVisuals.hole_rim_width": "Width of the glowing rim just outside a hole.",
"TerritoryVisuals.hole_rim_glow": "Emission strength of a hole's glowing rim.",
"TerritoryVisuals.flag_pole_height": "Height of a flag's pole.",
"TerritoryVisuals.flag_pole_radius": "Radius (thickness) of a flag's pole.",
"TerritoryVisuals.flag_pole_color": "Color of a flag's pole.",
"TerritoryVisuals.goal_flag_scale": "How much larger a goal flag's banner is than a home flag's.",
"TerritoryVisuals.goal_flag_color": "Color of a goal flag's banner.",
"TerritoryVisuals.flag_emission": "Emission strength of a flag's banner, so ownership reads at a glance.",
"TerritoryVisuals.capture_ring_radius": "Outer radius of the capture-progress ring shown on a goal flag while it's being captured.",
"TerritoryVisuals.capture_ring_thickness": "Thickness of the capture-progress ring.",
"TerritoryVisuals.capture_ring_lift": "Height above the disk surface the capture ring floats, to avoid z-fighting.",
"TerritoryVisuals.capture_ring_segments": "Segments in the full capture-ring circle; the drawn arc uses a proportional share.",
"TerritoryVisuals.capture_ring_emission": "Emission strength of the capture-progress ring.",
"TerritoryVisuals.rim_soft_width": "Half-width, in meters, of the blur applied to a territory's analytic circle edge.",
"TerritoryVisuals.rim_width": "Half-width, in meters, of the bright rim band drawn just inside a territory's analytic edge.",
"TerritoryVisuals.rim_strength": "Emission strength of the territory rim at the peak of its pulse.",
"TerritoryVisuals.rim_pulse_depth": "How much of the territory rim's pulse is animated versus a constant glow.",
"TerritoryVisuals.rim_speed": "Pulses per second along the territory rim.",
"TerritoryVisuals.metaball_blend": "Smooth-blend radius, in meters, used when overlapping same-team circles merge into one shape; 0 disables the blend.",
"TerritoryVisuals.max_shader_circles": "Maximum circles the territory shader draws per pixel before falling back to the raster path; lower this on weaker GPUs.",
"TerritoryVisuals.circle_bake_enabled": "Bake the territory circle field into a texture when it changes instead of looping circles per pixel; big GPU saving, turn off only to compare.",
"TerritoryVisuals.circle_bake_texels_per_m": "Resolution of the baked territory field in texels per meter; higher is crisper at the cost of a larger texture and bake.",
"TerritoryVisuals.reflection_probe_enabled": "Whether a ReflectionProbe over the disc mirrors placed blocks (not just the sky) in the disk's metallic surface.",
"TerritoryVisuals.reflection_probe_update_always": "Recompute the reflection probe every frame (blocks show up as they land, more GPU cost) instead of once at boot (cheap, but later blocks stay invisible in the reflection).",
"TerritoryVisuals.reflection_probe_margin_m": "Extra meters of box half-width the reflection probe extends beyond the largest map's radius.",
"TerritoryVisuals.reflection_probe_height_m": "Full box height, in meters, of the reflection probe above the disk.",
"TerritoryVisuals.ssr_enabled": "Whether screen-space reflections show currently-on-screen blocks mirrored in the disk, on top of the reflection probe.",
"TerritoryVisuals.ssr_max_steps": "Ray-march steps per pixel for screen-space reflections; higher finds thinner/further occluders at more GPU cost.",
"TerritoryVisuals.ssr_fade_in": "Meters of ray travel over which a screen-space reflection fades in, so it does not pop in sharply at the surface.",
"TerritoryVisuals.ssr_fade_out": "Meters of ray travel over which a screen-space reflection fades out toward the probe/sky fallback.",
"TerritoryVisuals.ssr_depth_tolerance": "Depth-buffer tolerance, in meters, for a screen-space reflection ray to count as hitting a surface.",
"TerritoryVisuals.mirror_enabled": "Whether a planar mirror camera renders a true per-pixel reflection of the scene onto the disk.",
"TerritoryVisuals.mirror_strength": "Fraction of the disk's color that is the planar mirror image; the rest is the lit disk/territory tint.",
"TerritoryVisuals.mirror_resolution_scale": "Planar mirror's render resolution as a fraction of the main viewport's; lower trades sharpness for GPU cost.",
"TerritoryVisuals.mirror_max_luminance": "Caps how bright the planar mirror's sampled color can be (hue preserved); the mirror is LDR, so only values below 1.0 dim anything.",
"TerritoryVisuals.mirror_sky_energy_scale": "How bright the sky/clouds render in the planar mirror camera's own Environment, as a fraction of the real scene's sky brightness; dims the sky in the reflection without touching how bright reflected blocks look.",
"TerritoryVisuals.mirror_center_fraction": "How strong the planar mirror stays looking straight down at the disc, as a fraction of mirror_strength; the fresnel term opens it up to the full mirror_strength at a grazing angle.",
"TerritoryVisuals.mirror_fresnel_power": "Fresnel exponent shaping how quickly the mirror blend opens from mirror_center_fraction to mirror_strength between straight-down and grazing camera angles.",
"BlockFeedConfig.min_stabilizers_per_bag": "Minimum stabilizing shapes guaranteed in every bag of blocks.",
"BlockFeedConfig.bag_multiplier": "How many copies of each shape's weight go into a bag; bigger means a longer, looser bag.",
"BlockFeedConfig.preview_count": "How many upcoming blocks the HUD shows in the feed preview.",
"BlockVisualTuning.outline_width_px": "Screen-space width, in pixels, of a nearby block's inverted-hull outline; constant at any distance up to outline_fade_start_m.",
"BlockVisualTuning.outline_far_width_px": "Outline width in pixels for blocks at or beyond outline_far_distance_m, so distant towers stay clean.",
"BlockVisualTuning.outline_fade_start_m": "Camera distance in meters where the block outline starts thinning toward its far width.",
"BlockVisualTuning.outline_far_distance_m": "Camera distance in meters where the block outline reaches its far width.",
"BlockVisualTuning.grid_line_far_cell_px": "On-screen cell size in pixels at or below which grid lines and bevels are at grid_line_far_strength.",
"BlockVisualTuning.grid_line_full_cell_px": "On-screen cell size in pixels at or above which grid lines and bevels are at full strength.",
"BlockVisualTuning.grid_line_far_strength": "Fraction of grid line/bevel strength kept when cells are tiny on screen (0 hides them, 1 disables the fade).",
"BlockVisualTuning.albedo_saturation": "Saturation multiplier on a block's colour before shading (1 = as authored).",
"BlockVisualTuning.cell_ao_strength": "Darkening at the bottom edge of each block cell face (contact shading); 0 disables it.",
"BlockVisualTuning.cell_ao_height": "Fraction of a cell face's height the bottom contact shading fades out over.",
"BlockVisualTuning.ambient_scale": "Scale of the sky ambient light on blocks; lower lets the cool toon shadow band dominate the shadow faces.",
"BlockVisualTuning.light_gain": "Overall gain on the block toon diffuse ramp.",
"BlockVisualTuning.band_softness": "Width of the anti-aliasing smoothstep at each toon band step.",
"BlockVisualTuning.bevel_shadow_side_fraction": "Fraction of the cell-edge bevel light kept on faces turned away from the sun.",
"BlockVisualTuning.rim_cool_color": "Color of the cool sky-bounce rim on block edges turned away from the sun.",
"BlockVisualTuning.rim_cool_strength": "Intensity of the cool sky-bounce rim on block edges turned away from the sun.",
"BlockVisualTuning.outline_color": "Flat, unshaded color of a block's outline pass.",
"BlockVisualTuning.toon_band_count": "How many discrete lit/shadow bands a block's toon diffuse ramp is quantized into.",
"BlockVisualTuning.grid_line_width_px": "Screen-space width, in pixels, of the dark line drawn along each visible cell face's edge.",
"BlockVisualTuning.grid_line_color": "Cell-grid line color for a block not currently read as contributing to territory influence.",
"BlockVisualTuning.grid_line_glow_color": "Cell-grid line color for a block that is settled/sleeping and so counted as contributing to territory influence.",
"BlockVisualTuning.grid_line_glow_strength": "Emission multiplier applied to the cell-grid glow color while a block is contributing.",
"BlockVisualTuning.grid_line_seam_mix": "How much of the grid line color to mix into the block's own albedo at a cell seam (0 = invisible, 1 = the old flat-replace black line).",
"BlockVisualTuning.highlight_tint": "Warm near-white blended into the brightest (top, sun-facing) toon band.",
"BlockVisualTuning.highlight_tint_mix": "How much of highlight_tint to blend into the brightest toon band.",
"BlockVisualTuning.highlight_brightness": "Extra brightness multiplier on the brightest toon band, applied after the highlight_tint blend.",
"BlockVisualTuning.lit_tint": "Warm, saturated tint blended lightly into the mid (lit-side) toon band.",
"BlockVisualTuning.lit_tint_mix": "How much of lit_tint to blend into the mid toon band.",
"BlockVisualTuning.shadow_tint": "Cool tint blended into the darkest (shadow) toon band before shadow_brightness dims it.",
"BlockVisualTuning.shadow_tint_mix": "How much of shadow_tint to blend into the darkest toon band.",
"BlockVisualTuning.shadow_brightness": "Brightness multiplier on the darkest toon band, kept above 0 so the shadow side never reads near-black.",
"BlockVisualTuning.specular_color": "Color of the block's hard-edged plastic specular highlight.",
"BlockVisualTuning.specular_sharpness": "Blinn-Phong exponent for the block's specular highlight before toon-quantizing; higher is a smaller, sharper dot.",
"BlockVisualTuning.specular_softness": "Width of the smoothstep that turns the block's specular falloff into a hard edge.",
"BlockVisualTuning.specular_strength": "Intensity multiplier of the block's specular highlight.",
"BlockVisualTuning.specular_albedo_tint": "How much of the block's own lit color to blend into the specular highlight instead of a flat white patch.",
"BlockVisualTuning.bevel_highlight_width_px": "Screen-space width, in pixels, the bright bevel band fades over starting at the true cell edge.",
"BlockVisualTuning.bevel_highlight_color": "Color of the bright bevel band hugging cell edges facing the light.",
"BlockVisualTuning.bevel_highlight_strength": "Intensity of the bright bevel band hugging cell edges facing the light.",
"BlockVisualTuning.rim_color": "Color of the subtle warm rim/Fresnel light on silhouette edges facing the sun.",
"BlockVisualTuning.rim_power": "Fresnel exponent for the rim light; higher narrows it to a thinner edge glow.",
"BlockVisualTuning.rim_strength": "Intensity of the rim light.",
"BlockVisualTuning.outline_tint_amount": "How much of a block's own (darkened) color to mix into its outline pass versus the flat outline_color.",
"BlockVisualTuning.outline_tint_darken": "How much a block's own color is darkened before being mixed into its outline pass.",
